True life: I caved yesterday and pre-ordered GTA VI. Not just the regular game, whatever stupid add-on “gotta have it” promotional pack they offered. I committed. I was in. I wanted to partake in the hype wave. It worked. I went to bed with a smile on my face. I was apart of something bigger than myself. The movement. 

To wake up and see how bad this game is has felt like the equivalent to some snot nose kid at school telling you Santa isn’t real when you just wanted to have the magic for one more year. 

@RockstarGames wtf is going on!!!! Chores as a game? We want bang bang shoot shoot. It’s not complicated. This isn’t the Sims.

